    {
     "text": ". "
    },
    {
     "text": "A ",
     "bold": true
    },
    {
     "text": "z",
     "bold": true,
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": "-score is measured in units of the standard deviation.",
     "bold": true
    },
    {
     "text": " For example, if the mean of a normal distribution is five and the standard deviation is two, the value 11 is three standard deviations above (or to the right of) the mean. The calculation is as follows:"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "spans": [
    {
     "text": "x",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": " = "
    },
    {
     "text": "μ",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": " + ("
    },
    {
     "text": "z",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": ")("
    },
    {
     "text": "σ",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": ") = 5 + (3)(2) = 11"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "spans": [
    {
     "text": "The "
    },
    {
     "text": "z",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": "-score is three."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "spans": [
    {
     "text": "The mean for the standard normal distribution is zero, and the standard deviation is one. The transformation "
    },
    {
     "text": "z",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": " = "
    },
    {
     "text": "x−µσ",
     "latex": "\\frac{x - \\mu}{\\sigma}"
    },
    {
     "text": " produces the distribution "
    },
    {
     "text": "Z",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": " ~ "
    },
    {
     "text": "N",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": "(0, 1). The value "
    },
    {
     "text": "x",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": " in the given equation comes from a normal distribution with mean "
    },
    {
     "text": "μ",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": " and standard deviation "
    },
    {
     "text": "σ",
     "italic": true
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
